<name>Power Window System</name>
<para id="RM0000005DY00JX" category="J" type-id="30309" name-id="752B7-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Operates after key OFF even when operating conditions are not met</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005DY00JX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000025A00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If the driver side door has not been opened and then fully closed within approximately 45 seconds after the IG is turned from ON to OFF, the power window regulator motor assembly receives an operation permission signal from the body ECU with power source ECU and can control the door glass of its own seat. When approximately 45 seconds have elapsed or the driver side door being opened and then fully closed is detected, operation stops after the key is turned OFF.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The power window system uses the Body Electronics Area Network. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" to perform the "communication function inspection" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The power window system prohibits AUTO operation if there is a malfunction in the jam protection function, so confirm that the diagnostic trouble codes are normal before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
